A||||8||88 Fiero||Finally!!! been in a test drive on a 1988 3.4 Turbocharge Intercooled Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||88 Fiero||04-11-2000||01:16 AM||||Well...swing by last night at Fiero Docs Shop to see what's going on. He said that he just finished working on Bob Yorks '88 Automatic Red Fiero GT and he asked me for a ride with this beast. Mannnn!!!! talk about acceleration...This car got a different gearing in auto-tranny. We test run the car without activating the water-cooled intercooler and with the intercooler running... The car was wicked and quick!!! Comparing it with the Design One Turbo on a 2.8 V6...totally different and I mean different...It's like night and day difference...I mean I was speechless and am looking forward to do a 3.4 on my car. The turbo that is being used came from a 300ZX. Everything is custom on that car. I have a tubo unit which is the same as the Design One and probably will be changing to a different Turbo Unit...So everyone with an existing turbo...swap with the 3.4 and you'll be smiling from ear to ear.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||04-11-2000||09:56 AM||||Better have big pockets.  I doubt it's cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||04-11-2000||10:35 AM||||88 Fiero, I've always had the idea of swapping the 2.8 for the 3.4 in my 86SE. I'd use the existing MillerWoods turbo on the 3.4 (after a quick freshen-up!). But, at least at this time there's no point, the 2.8 has barely over 51K miles, and runs perfect! No problems! That turbo is there everytime I need it! Sometimes I feel it's too fast for me!!  <BR>Of course, I could always buy that 86GT with an engine knock, put my 2.8 in that, find a good 3.4, put the turbo on it.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||88 Fiero||04-11-2000||10:58 AM||||Like you turbo...I also have the MillerWoods Turbo not installed yet... My mileage on my car is about 80,000 miles and it's still very healthy... I am waiting for it to get tired so I can go with the 3.4 specially now that I experienced the E-ticket ride...One thing that I am considering is replacing the IHI turbo with something else...maybe a unit from Turbonetics...||||reg||1
Z||000004||jhogans||04-11-2000||12:20 PM||||Are you guys referring to the 3.4 TDC?||||reg||1
Z||000005||VISCERAL||04-11-2000||01:38 PM||||Hey 88 fiero you need to enlighten us on the details of the parts list, what you/they use, <BR>pics, example price list, etc... thanks<P>Or does it follow Lagrua's method of turbo design?<P>I've considered a 3.4 turbo, mpfi 4.3, mpfi turbo 4.3, or just v8.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||04-11-2000||01:57 PM||||Visceral...actually the turbo that Bob York bought came from IFG. It blew his engine. So he took it to Fiero Doc to work on it. Fiero Doc says that he will bring the car to the show..I dont know which one tho...but it's very wicked...we tested it in a business complex on the street...we were going about 6 to 7 lbs of boost and the car was set for 10 lbs. of boost...run out of runway...but it's very, very quick and it spools real fast...we even burn rubber and it left a 6 foot skidmark....I will try and take pictures of the car once I get hold of a digital camera...||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||04-11-2000||07:51 PM||||I went on a test drive in an 84 coupe with a supercharged 3.8 that had 285HP. The guy could not mat the throttle because he had a bad motor mount. That coupe pushed me into the seat like nothing I've ever felt before with only a little more than half throttle and he didn't even build any boost because of the bad motor mount. He had it in fifth gear going 40mph (5 speed Trans) and it still would push you if you gave it the throttle, my 2.8 would just bog in fifth @ 40mph. That supercharged 3.8 was all low end torque and a ton of fun to drive. <P>Where do you guys get the MillerWoods turbo?<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||04-11-2000||10:47 PM||||Bob already has it registered for San Diego. A T3 turbo takes the charge and goes through a custom air to water intercooler using a radiator on the passenger side intake. The intercooler as well as the resevoir are both triple chromed and in the trunk as well as the water injection unit. Water injection come on at 7 lbs of boost. It is a 3.4 V6 from the 91-95 F-bodies with extensive headwork, roller chain cam shaft roller tip rockers and custom headers for the turbo. We were taking it out and running it through more paces and everything looks like a go for San Diego! The part I love the best is the "Fieros West" decal on the passenger side of the windshield, but Im just biased that way....||||reg||1
